  "generation": {
    "prompt": "Animation contact sheet for the style bible version 2026-11-08-stevie-strips.\nSubject: stevie, an adult raccoon exactly as in the approved turnaround: grey-brown fur with a lighter tan underside, a black eye mask with white brows and a white muzzle, rounded ears with pale rims, dark brown legs and paws, and a bushy ringed tail with dark brown and tan bands.\nDraw one complete \"idle\" animation cycle of 6 frames, as a sprite sheet of 3 columns and 2 rows of equal cells, frames in reading order (left to right, then top to bottom); leave any cell after the last frame empty.\nThe same character in every frame: identical design, colours, proportions and scale. One whole, uncropped figure per cell, centred in its cell, with the feet on the same ground line in every cell. Consecutive frames change only the pose, so the last frame flows back into the first.\nEach frame will be scaled to a 192x192 px game frame, so keep the silhouette readable.\nReference images, in order: approved character turnaround (front, three-quarter, side, back), approved three-quarter view, perspective sample, palette swatch. Match the identity to the subject references and the camera angle to the perspective sample.\nPalette: #1e1b19, #2f2722, #6c6259, #8e8274, #b39a7a, #e4ddd0, #d9a157, #5f7488.\nPaint albedo under a neutral key light, without baked directional shadows, highlights or emissive glow.\nMood: quiet, warm, storybook.\nStyle note: Painterly storybook illustration: soft visible brushwork, fine fur texture, soft feathered fur edges, no ink outlines. Not pixel art, not flat vector, not 3D render.\nStyle note: Camera: the same high three-quarter view from above as the perspective sample, so the back and the far side of the body are partly visible and the paws sit on a ground plane seen from above.\nStyle note: The world's lighting is warm lamplight against cool blue dusk rain; the game applies that light, so keep the fur colours true to the turnaround.\nStyle note: The idle cycle: Stevie stands still on all four paws, body facing the lower left in three-quarter view, and only breathes: a slow rise and fall of the back and chest, a slight sway of the tail tip and one small ear flick. Paws never move.\nPlain flat uniform light background across the whole sheet, no grid lines, no borders, no text, no numbers, no shadow on the ground.",
    "parameters": {
      "animationFamily": "idle",
      "requestedFrames": 6,
